<newsitem itemid="52477" id="root" date="1996-09-13" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Decor lifts year shr, div increased.</title>
<headline>Decor lifts year shr, div increased.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, attrib (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre exceptional items     21.04	vs    14.04</p>
<p>    - after exceptional items   21.77	vs    14.12</p>
<p>    Div (cts)	     6.50 making 9	vs    4.00</p>
<p>    Attrib income		    4.15	vs    2.47</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			    4.42	vs    2.50</p>
<p>    Tax				  0.25	vs    0.03</p>
<p>    Interest paid		    0.53	vs    0.10</p>
<p>    Turnover			  20.35	vs    16.75</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     0.14	   vs    0.01</p>
<p>Div payable October 25</p>
<p>on register October 4</p>
<p>Full name: Decor Investment Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said although its prospects were constrained by the slowdown in business activity, it was anticipated that at least the current level of profitability would be maintained.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
